"eda4714816f93c2e7172736ea58df1774bdbbf22": {"body":"As of 21:01 UTC: Lisbon's orange sea ended at 21:00 (s-1111T2100); yellow sea to 03:00.\nNew section 'Forecast beside observations' (rain, wind, track, timing, sea, Madeira, who was\nunder red), with three lessons as hypotheses (CAP ahead of open data; the press repeating\nsuperseded warnings; no sea observation of our own). Lead: the storm has passed (fact),\nwhat Lisbon got (about 110 mm at Relogio, 74 km/h gust; fact), ANEPC's 1,630 occurrences and\nabout 400 flights (evidence). Decisions to the stand-down (Lusoponte, Transtejo back to normal;\nCP; the PM and ANEPC as evidence). tools/brief-make.mjs: E.after, E.lessons, E.gaps_title,\nE.rain_hours. Editions 1-9 unchanged.","session":"session_018yvwtPVWJtSb1BoAg7xMvW","files":[{"p":"brief/README.md","a":6,"d":5},{"p":"brief/brief.css","a":2,"d":0},{"p":"brief/edition-10.json","a":286,"d":0},{"p":"brief/edition-10.md","a":24,"d":0},{"p":"tools/brief-make.mjs","a":5,"d":4}],"more_files":0},
